// ============================================================
// History Domain (L4) — the partitioned trade store
// ============================================================
// The same trades as trading::Trade, reached through a union over three partitions
// instead of a single table. Whatever the physical layout, the answer must not change —
// which makes this the second independent invariance in the corpus, orthogonal to L2's:
// L2 varies how a row is ASSEMBLED (join vs denormalized), L4 varies where rows COME FROM.
###Pure
Class trading::HistTrade
{
    tradeId: String[1];
    tradeDate: StrictDate[1];
    quantity: Float[1];
    price: Float[1];
    notional: Float[1];
    side: trading::Side[1];
    status: String[1];
    currency: String[1];
}
